# Step 11.3 — Connect the Five Existing SentinelAI Investigation Tools

The Java ADK Gemini agent from Step 11.2 is already created under agent/ and is isolated from the existing Spring Boot backend.

Now connect the five existing SentinelAI investigation tools to the Java ADK agent.

Existing tools:
1. getServiceHealth()
2. getPaymentMetrics(startTime, endTime)
3. getKafkaConsumerLag(consumerGroup, topic)
4. getRecentErrors(service, timeWindow)
5. getDependencyHealth()

Requirements:
- First inspect the existing Spring Boot backend and locate the already implemented tool interfaces/endpoints/classes.
- Do not redesign or replace the existing tools.
- Do not change the existing backend architecture.
- Keep all five tools read-only.
- The agent must receive real responses from the existing backend, not hard-coded/mock investigation data.
- Use the appropriate Java ADK Function Tool mechanism supported by the currently installed google-adk version.
- Keep the agent isolated under agent/.
- Use the existing backend APIs/contracts where applicable.
- Do not add unnecessary dependencies or frameworks.
- Do not add Gemini instructions yet.
- Do not implement the complete investigation flow yet.
- Do not implement RCA generation yet.
- Do not store investigation results yet.
- Do not expose GOOGLE_API_KEY.
- Do not modify unrelated backend functionality.

Acceptance criteria:
- All five tools are exposed to the ADK agent.
- Each tool can obtain real data from the existing backend.
- Tool failures are surfaced rather than fabricated.
- Existing Spring Boot functionality continues to work.
- Maven build succeeds.

After implementation report:
1. Files changed.
2. How each of the five tools is connected.
3. Backend endpoint/class used by each tool.
4. Dependencies added, if any.
5. Build/test result.
6. Any blocker or API limitation.

Stop after the five tools are connected successfully.